+### Web-search engine policy
+
+The `[websearch].engine` setting is an ordered allowlist. It accepts the
+historical scalar form or the canonical array form, for example
+`engine = ["searxng", "bing"]`. Engines are attempted in listed order, and a
+websearch request cannot select or prioritize an engine outside that list. The
+default order remains DuckDuckGo followed by Bing. The deprecated
+`fallback_engines` setting is still read and appended during migration.
+
+`JCODE_WEBSEARCH_ENGINES` replaces the complete ordered list. The compatible
+`JCODE_WEBSEARCH_ENGINE` override replaces only the primary engine while
+retaining the configured tail. Invalid or empty engine overrides fail strict
+configuration loading.
+
 ---
 
